#. type: Title #
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Hamiltonian simulation {#hamiltonian-simulation}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Hamiltonian simulation is a quantum computing technique used to model and "
"characterize quantum systems based on their energy and interactions. It has "
"potential applications in drug discovery and chemistry, battery development,"
" catalyst design, advanced materials, solar energy, and the study of complex"
" physical phenomena such as superconductivity. \n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"By simulating molecular interactions and the behavior of electrons and "
"atoms, Hamiltonian simulation can help researchers predict material "
"properties, understand chemical reactions, and identify promising candidates"
" for new technologies. Common approaches include Trotterization, which "
"approximates continuous time evolution using sequences of quantum gates, and"
" sample based quantum diagonalization, which estimates the energy spectrum "
"for a given quantum system.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A typical workflow starts by mapping a physical system, such as a set of "
"interacting fermions or bosons, onto qubits and circuits. From there, you "
"can reduce the resulting circuit's depth and gate count with compilation and"
" error-mitigation techniques, run the circuit on quantum hardware, and "
"reconstruct the system's properties, such as its ground-state energy, from "
"the measured samples. The tools on this page cover each of these stages, and"
" the application functions listed here provides a single managed workflow "
"for Hamiltonian simulation.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Mapping tools {#mapping-tools}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These capabilities specialize in mapping domain problems into quantum operators and circuits for execution on a quantum computer. Use them to represent fermionic, bosonic, or spin systems, and to compile the resulting circuits so that they run with less depth and fewer entangling gates on quantum hardware.\n"
"<CardGroup>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    <Card\n"
"      title=\"Qiskit Fermions\"\n"
"      description=\"Work with fermionic systems using data structures for fermionic operators and circuits, as well as frameworks for fermion-to-qubit encodings and circuit synthesis through the Qiskit transpiler integration.\"\n"
"      href=\"/addons/qiskit-fermions\"\n"
"      analyticsName=\"Documentation page: Qiskit Fermions\"\n"
"      linkText=\"Browse documentation\"\n"
"    />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
